## Key Findings

- 3 novel pan-cancer SL genes at FDR<0.05: SUCO (d=-0.82), EID3 (d=-0.74), SLC33A1 (d=-0.72)
- ER-resident vulnerability cluster (SUCO, SLC33A1, TAPT1) cross-validated by independent CRISPR screen
- UXS1/pyrimidine axis: large lineage effects (d=-0.5 to -1.0) but not FDR-significant; NRF2-UXS1 correlation r=-0.445 (p=0.003) strongest evidence
- ATR: null CRISPR/PRISM signal (expected for essential gene); clinical hypothesis from HUDSON trial remains
- 0/6790 PRISM compounds selectively sensitize KEAP1-mutant cells — broad drug resistance validated
- DRP-104 (glutamine antagonist) Phase 2 enrolling — first KEAP1-directed trial
- HERC2/UBR4/HUWE1 E3 ligases (EMBO J 2026) NOT replicated in DepMap
- Success criteria: 2/5 met, 1 inconclusive, 2 not met

